|passage=''Tony'': I was not.<br>''Sidney'': Don’t give me that old '''codswallop'''. You were counting your money.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=October 17 1963|journal=w:Radio Times|section=52/2
|passage=Just branding a programme as ‘rubbish’, ‘tripe’, or—there are a lot of these—‘'''codswallop'''’, gives little indication of what moved the viewer to write.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=October 1 1981|author=John Turner|title=Review: Autumn Books: Prometheus bounded?|journal=w:New Scientist|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=EIZI3TDTGTsC&pg=PA41&dq=%22codswallop%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=XBwtT6-WMYzqmAXgo82DDQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22codswallop%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=41
|passage=An interviewer from a Warsaw radio station stopped a citizen in the street. Was the recent demonstration necessary? “History will tell.” But what did he think? “I am not a historian.” Likewise Lumsden′s and Wilson′s book. If it is not a load of '''codswallop''', it will turn out to be very important. If it is not a load of '''codswallop'''. ''Faites vos jeux!''}}
#* '''1993''', J. Neville Turner, ''The One-Day Game – Cricket or '''Codswallop'''?'', in 2001, David John Headon, ''The Best Ever Australian Sports Writing: A 200 Year Collection''.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author=Grahame Howard|title=The Wishing Book 3 – Extermination|page=66|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=3sAk0FUDueUC&pg=PA66&dq=%22codswallop%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=2xgtT5_rGeeNmQXd0bDqDw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22codswallop%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|passage=“I′ve told you all I know,” Rosa Armaz told Boarski and Yermin, “I don′t know what my husband has been doing. He′d mentioned going to Mars with the children but I thought it was a load of '''codswallop'''.”}}

